Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:58:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] GS (OpenGL): framebuffers taller than 1024 lines, and
 textures and displays inside them

- Framebuffers are as tall as the GS memory after them allows (up to 2048 lines,
  within what CGsCachedArea tracks), as games draw below line 1024.
- A texture may start at any page inside a framebuffer, not only on its first
  line of pages, and clamping follows the offset.
- A displayed buffer that starts inside a taller framebuffer is shown from it.

Midnight Club: its intro video and title screen were black or scrambled.
